;; any-widen-stored-in-an-adt-field-has-no-owner: a value widened into an `:any`
;; FIELD mallocs a box, and nothing used to free it.
;;
;; `any-struct-box-leak-per-widen` gave every `any` payload box an owner across
;; five passes -- an argument, a local, a temporary, past an early exit, a
;; narrowed binding -- and every one of those owners is a SCOPE.  A box stored
;; into a field outlives every scope they can attach a drop to, correctly so,
;; and therefore had none.  A container with `any` elements pays one leak per
;; element.
;;
;; The drop is `__tur_any_drop`, not a statically-named glue, and that is the
;; whole reason an `:any` field could not reuse the machinery the recursive and
;; nested-aggregate fields use: the payload's type is whatever the tag says at
;; run time.  The registry row already carries the `boxed` flag the widen wrote,
;; so an `any` field holding an int frees nothing and one holding a widened
;; aggregate frees the box -- decided by the same row, at run time.
;;
;; `Pt` is `:copy` so the widened value is an ordinary by-value aggregate (the
;; shape that actually allocates); `Box` is NOT `:copy`, which is the soundness
;; line -- drop glue makes it move-only, and that move discipline is the
;; single-owner guarantee the free depends on.  Under `:copy` two values could
;; share the box and a per-owner free would free it twice.
;;
;; requires.leak-check: the assertion is about allocation, not output.  The
;; printed value is the same either way, which is why this leaked unnoticed.

(defdata ^copy Pt [] (P [x : int y : int]))
(defdata Box [] (B [v : any]) (Nil))

(defn main [] : int
  ;; A non-escaping local owning an `any` field: the box is released when the
  ;; scope exits.  A `Box` handed to a helper is MOVED instead, and nothing
  ;; discharges it there yet -- the residue the report tracks.
  (let [b (B (:: (P 1 2) any))]
    (println (match b
               (B v)  1
               (Nil)  0)))
  ;; An `any` field holding a carrier payload allocates nothing, so the drop
  ;; must be a no-op rather than a free of a non-pointer: __tur_any_drop reads
  ;; the registry row for the tag, which says boxed=0 for an int.
  (let [c (B (:: 7 any))]
    (println (match c
               (B v)  2
               (Nil)  0)))
  0)
